unstructured">American Academy of Pain Medicine and American Pain Society. The use of opioids for the treatment of chronic pain. A consensus statement. Clin J Pain. 1997;13:6&#x02013;8. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9084947</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="other">Guidelines for the assessment and management of chronic pain. Wisconsin Medical Society Taskforce on Pain Management. WMJ. 2004;103(3):15&#x02013;42.</citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Donovan</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Evers</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mandleblatt</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>When there is no benchmark: designing a primary care-based chronic pain management program from the scientific basis up</article-title><source>J Pain Symptom Manage</source><year>1999</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>38</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0885-3924(99)00021-4</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Donovan MI, Evers K, Jacobs P, Mandleblatt S. When there is no benchmark: designing a primary care-based chronic pain management program from the scientific basis up. J Pain Symptom Manage. 1999;18:38&#x02013;48. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10439571</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Quill</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Partnerships in patient care: a contractual approach</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>1983</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>228</fpage><lpage>234</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Quill TE. Partnerships in patient care: a c