-type="display-unstructured">Robinson RC, et al. Screening for problematic prescription opioid use. Clin J Pain. 2001;17(3):220&#x02013;5. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11587112</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR23"><label>23.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chabel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Erjavec</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobson</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prescription opiate abuse in chronic pain patients: clinical criteria, incidence, and predictors (see comments)</article-title><source>Clin J Pain</source><year>1997</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>150</fpage><lpage>155</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00002508-199706000-00009</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Chabel C, Erjavec MK, Jacobson L, et al. Prescription opiate abuse in chronic pain patients: clinical criteria, incidence, and predictors (see comments). Clin J Pain. 1997;12:150&#x02013;5. </citation></ref><ref id="CR24"><label>24.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Osterberg</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Blaschke</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Adherence to medication</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>353</volume><fpage>487</fpage><lpage>497</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJMra050100</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Osterberg L, Blaschke T. Adherence to medication. N Engl J Med. 2005;353:487&#x02013;97. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16079372</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR25"><label>25.</label><citation citation-type="other"><bold>Katz N, Fanciullo GJ.</bold> Role of urine toxicology testing in the management of chronic opioid therapy. Clin J Pain. 2002;18(4)(suppl):S76&#x02013;S82.</citation></ref><ref id="CR26"><label>26.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heit</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gourlay</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Urine drug testing in pain medicine</article-title><source>J Pain Symptom Manage</source><year>2004</year><volume>27</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>260</fpage><lpage>267</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jpainsymman.2003.07.008</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Heit HA, Gourlay DL. Urine drug testing in pain medicine. J Pain Symptom Manage. 2004;27(3):260&#x02013;7. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15010104</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR27"><label>27.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Katz</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Behavioral monitoring and urine toxicology testing in patients receiving long-term opioid therapy</article-title><source>Anesth Analg</source><year>2003</year><volume>97</volume><fpage>1097</fpage><lpage>1102</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1213/01.ANE.0000080159.83342.B5</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Katz NP, et al. Behavioral monitoring and urine toxicology testing in patients receiving long-term opioid therapy. Anesth Analg. 2003;97:1097&#x02013;102. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14500164</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>